    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260821001": {
      "title": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (two posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (two posts) (Ref. 260821001) In line with the strategic development of the University and to lead the development of the aeronautical and aviation engineering discipline in teaching and research activities, the Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering was established in the Faculty of Engineering. The Department currently offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and actively engages in various research and consultancy work. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/aae/ for more information about the Department. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU’s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.  Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. The Department is seeking highly motivated and suitably qualified individuals with research expertise in AI/Robotics for Aircraft Maintenance / Low-Altitude Economy / Satellite and Space Engineering and applications are now invited from academics who are actively involved in the aforementioned strategic research track to fill the vacancies for academic staff under Strategic Hiring Scheme. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in the aforementioned strategic research areas.  Beyond these primary areas, the candidate should be prepared to contribute to multidisciplinary subjects; (b)    conduct research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; (c)    attract research fundings and support industrial researches; (d)    supervise student projects and theses; (e)    engage in scholarly research/consultancy in their area of expertise; (f)     contribute to departmental services and activities; and (g)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a doctoral degree in Engineering with expertise in (1) AI/Robotics for aircraft maintenance, including but not limited to predictive maintenance, digital twins, conditional monitoring, robots for inspection and repairing; (2) in satellite and space engineering, including but not limited to spacecraft dynamics and control, payload and instrumentation, space robots, spacecraft design and tests, space technology applications such as navigation, remote sensing, and communications; or (3) in low-altitude economy, including but not limited to unmanned aerial vehicles, advanced air mobility, perception, autonomous control, decision making, unmanned air traffic management, and applications (e.g. transportation, inspection, search and rescue, etc.); (b)    have the relevant postdoctoral research experience and a publication record that is commensurate with the level of appointment; (c)    demonstrate excellence in original research and strong fundamental knowledge in one or more of the above-mentioned core research areas; (d)    demonstrate potential to establish significant externally funded research programmes; (e)    be able to demonstrate evidence of effective classroom teaching skills; and (f)    have excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 September 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 21 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260820014": {
      "title": "Job Application - Instructor (Temporary Appointment)  (two posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Instructor (Temporary Appointment)  (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Chinese History and Culture Instructor (Temporary Appointment)  (two posts) (Ref. 260820014) [Appointment period: each for twelve months initially, with possibility of further appointment] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    engage in teaching aspects of Chinese History and Culture and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b)    engage in programme/curriculum design and development, consultancy projects and other scholarly activities that help promote the department’s interests; (c)    provide administrative support for academic and departmental affairs; (d)    assist in organising student activities/training workshops to enhance students’ learning experience; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in History or a relevant discipline; (b)    at least one year of relevant post-qualification teaching experience at the tertiary level; (c)    an excellent command of both English and Chinese (Putonghua), with fluency in Cantonese being an advantage; and (d)    a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in the fields of History, Literature, and Science and Technology. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 2 September 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 20 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260818012": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Language Neuroscience and Neurotechnology",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Language Neuroscience and Neurotechnology Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Language Science and Technology Assistant Professor in Language Neuroscience and Neurotechnology (Ref. 260818012) The Department of Language Science and Technology (LST) is an academic unit within the Faculty of Humanities dedicated to the scientific study of language in all its facets. With a team over 70 committed academic and teaching/clinical staff members, our work spans from investigating the biological and cognitive foundations of language to its societal function in multilingual environments and its transformation through technology. The Department pursues interdisciplinary research that integrates core language science domains such as artificial intelligence and big data analytics, with applications in communication, education and healthcare. Alongside research activities, the Department actively translates scholarly insights into practice through clinical services, educational outreach and technology development that serve both local and international communities. The Department houses several specialised units, including the Speech Therapy Unit, the Research Centre for Language, Cognition and Neuroscience, and the Centre for Translation Studies, which serve as vital hubs for both research and practical application. More information about the Department can be found at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/lst/ . The Department invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position. We seek a scholar with strong expertise in integrating neuroscience and neurotechnology with language and speech data using computational approaches, including artificial intelligence, machine learning and deep learning, and a demonstrated commitment to translating research into clinical practice. We are particularly interested in candidates who: •  design and develop computational AI, machine learning or deep learning architectures to model language and speech processes at the neural level; •  use neurotechnological tools [e.g., EEG, MEG, fMRI, fNIRS, TMS, tDCS or brain-computer interfaces (BCI)] to investigate language and speech in typical and clinical populations; •  have a strong track record of research in language neuroscience, speech-language pathology or related fields, with clear clinical applications (e.g., aphasia, dyslexia, developmental language disorders or other communication and neurological conditions); and •  demonstrate excellence in translating research into clinical tools, neuro-rehabilitation protocols, assistive technologies, or digital therapeutics. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    contribute to the teaching/learning activities for the Department at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and supervise student projects and theses; (b)    lead and/or participate in the planning, management and curriculum development; (c)    develop e-learning modules and design innovative pedagogy; (d)    secure external competitive research grants, conduct academic research, publish in top-tier refereed journals, and provide academic leadership in teaching, research and other scholarly activities; (e)    foster research collaborations both locally and internationally; (f)    engage the industries in high-level, impact-rich consultancies; (g)    carry out academic and administrative duties; and (h)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    hold a PhD degree in a relevant field, such as Neuroscience, Linguistics, Cognitive Science, Speech-Language Pathology, Biomedical Engineering, Computer Science or a closely related field; (b)    demonstrate expertise in neuroscience and neurotechnology, as evidenced by publications and research experience using one or more of the following: •  Neuroimaging (e.g., f/MRI, EEG/MEG, fNIRS or ECoG); •  Neuromodulation (e.g., TMS, tDCS/tACs or DBS); •  Brain-Computer Interfaces (BCI) or assistive neurotechnologies; •  Computational modelling of neural signals; (c)    have a strong track record in designing and developing AI, machine learning, or deep learning models for language or speech data; (d)    have evidence of clinical translation or strong potential to translate research into clinical practice (e.g., aphasia, dyslexia, developmental language disorders or other communication and neurological conditions); (e)    have experience in teaching and curriculum development, with a willingness to contribute to programme planning and management; (f)    have a strong track record of publishing in high-quality international journals as a first or corresponding author, and demonstrated potential to secure competitive external research funding; (g)    be open to the use of e-learning and blended learning strategies in teaching and scholarship; and (h)    have good networking ability and interdisciplinary collaboration skills. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 17 September 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 18 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260817003": {
      "title": "Job Application - Clinical Associate in Radiography",
      "description": "Job Application - Clinical Associate in Radiography Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Health Technology and Informatics Clinical Associate in Radiography (Ref. 260817003) [will be conferred the title of Assistant Professor of Practice] Building on over 40 years of educational excellence in Hong Kong, the Department of Health Technology and Informatics (HTI) advances world-class teaching and research in four key medical fields (4M): Medical Laboratory Science, Medical Imaging & Radiation Science, Medical Physics, and Medical Data Science. HTI cultivates future leaders with both professional expertise and scientific vision, fostering an inclusive learning environment that produces top graduates for Asia and beyond. At the forefront of innovation, HTI drives impactful research and technological breakthroughs in the 4M areas. Through cutting-edge scientific discovery and collaborations with leading global institutions, we deliver groundbreaking innovations with profound societal impact. Explore more: www.polyu.edu.hk/hti Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    teach undergraduate/postgraduate courses and supervise students in their clinical training; (b)    perform other teaching support functions such as supervising students in projects and seminars; (c)    contribute to programme planning, administration and development; (d)    engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (e)    carry out academic and administrative duties as required; and (f)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a higher degree in Medical Imaging and Radiation Science (MIRS) or a related discipline; (b)    a qualification registrable with the Radiographers Board of the HKSAR; and (c)    not less than five years of post-registration clinical experience in Radiography. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 24 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 17 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260811002": {
      "title": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Rehabilitation Sciences Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Occupational Therapy (Ref. 260811002) The Department of Rehabilitation Sciences offers teaching programmes from entry-level BSc (Hons) to PhD for Occupational Therapy and Physiotherapy.  There are over 70 faculty members in the disciplines of Occupational Therapy, Physiotherapy and Rehabilitation Sciences in the Department.  The main translational research programmes in the Department are Better Ageing and Longevity, Intelligent Rehabilitation, Musculoskeletal and Sports Science, Neuroscience as well as Primary Healthcare and Lifestyle Medicine.  It also operates a Rehabilitation Clinic which is the hub for clinical teaching and consultancy services to the community.  The Department puts equal emphases on basic, applied and clinical research relevant to the theory and technology development in rehabilitation.  Besides, the Department has taken the lead in incorporating Chinese therapeutics into the academic curricula which is unique worldwide.  The vision of the Department is “ To build a future where individuals of all ages and abilities thrive through innovative rehabilitation ”.  For more information about the Department, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/rs/ . Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching in undergraduate and postgraduate programmes including supervision of student projects and seminars and/or supervision of clinical placements; (b)    carry out independent research and other scholarly activities and obtain research grants; (c)    participate in community, professional and/or consultancy services; (d)    undertake administrative duties; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Occupational Therapy and/or Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline; (b)    a strong commitment to excellence in teaching with demonstrated good teaching performance; (c)    a promising research and publication record with expertise of translational research in artificial intelligence, virtual reality, digital technologies or other emerging technologies relevant to rehabilitation and healthcare innovation; and (d)    good interpersonal and communication skills. Applicants with proven excellence in translational research and teaching may be considered for appointment at Associate Professor level or above. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 25 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 11 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260810008": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Chinese History and Culture Teaching Fellow (Ref. 260810008) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] The Department of Chinese History and Culture is an academic department within the Faculty of Humanities.  Its mission is to offer high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate programmes that provide interdisciplinary training in the study of Chinese history and culture. Currently, the Department offers PhD and MPhil programmes, a taught-master degree programme, a major degree programme in Chinese History and Culture, a minor degree programme in Chinese History and Culture, and university-wide general education courses.  The media of instruction are English and Putonghua.  Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/chc/ for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    engage in teaching Chinese history and culture and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b)    engage in programme/curriculum design and development, consultancy projects and other scholarly activities that help promote the department’s interests; (c)    provide administrative support for academic and departmental affairs; and (d)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in a relevant discipline; (b)    at least three years of relevant post-qualification tertiary teaching experience; (c)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning; and (d)    an excellent command of both English and Chinese. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 24 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 10 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260810006": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Marketing (Consumer Behavior)",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Marketing (Consumer Behavior) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Management and Marketing Assistant Professor in Marketing (Consumer Behavior) (Ref. 260810006) The Department of Management and Marketing (MM) is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Business.  MM is dedicated to providing cutting-edge knowledge and practical skills for our students in three key areas of business — Management , Marketing , and Management Information Systems .  MM offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Science, and Bachelor of Business Administration.  MM currently has around 60 full-time academic staff who are actively involved in research, consultancy, and management development work with businesses in Hong Kong, the Chinese mainland, and internationally.  MM is committed to excellence in teaching, research and service to the community. The Marketing discipline of the Department invites applications for faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, in the area of Consumer Behavior .  The faculty members in the Marketing discipline of MM regularly publish their research in top-tier refereed marketing journals such as the Journal of Consumer Research, Journal of Marketing Research, Journal of Marketing, and Marketing Science .  Research-focused applicants who are interested in joining our vibrant and growing research team are strongly encouraged to apply for the post. Please visit the website at https://mm.polyu.edu.hk/ for more information about MM.  Applicants are invited to contact Professor Yuwei Jiang, Chair Professor and Associate Head of MM by email at yuwei.jiang@polyu.edu.hk for further information about the post. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    engage in top-level scholarly research in their areas of expertise; (b)    supervise research students; (c)    secure external competitive research grants; (d)    teach at the undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Marketing or a relevant discipline at the time of appointment or be close to receiving it; and (b)    a strong research orientation and the potential to publish in high quality scholarly journals. Conditions of Service The compensation package, teaching loads, and research support are highly competitive.  Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 1 September 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 10 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260803003": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Applied Social Sciences Assistant Professor in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy (Ref. 260803003) As one of the largest social sciences departments in the Asian Pacific region, the Department of Applied Social Sciences offers research degrees at MPhil and PhD levels as well as taught programmes at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in various disciplines. The Department is home to many thriving research and practice units: Centre for Social Policy and Social Entrepreneurship, Child Development Centre, China and Global Development Network, and Professional Practice and Assessment Centre.  It is also strongly connected with the Institute of Active Ageing of the Faculty of Health and Social Sciences and other health related disciplines.  They provide platforms for collaborative research, practice projects, and policy discussions with government departments and NGOs.  Focused areas of research in the Department include but not limited to: (a) family, child, youth and ageing studies; (b) psychology, mental health, and health; (c) social work and human service management; (d) social policy, social welfare, and community development; and (e) social theory, and the Chinese Mainland and global social development. Please visit the website at http://www.polyu.edu.hk/apss/ for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) teach subjects in the discipline of Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy and/or related subjects; (b) contribute to the development and enhancement of teaching and learning; (c) lead and/or participate in the planning, management and curriculum development of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes; (d) develop e-learning modules and design innovative pedagogy; (e) secure external competitive research grants, conduct academic research, publish in good quality peer-reviewed journals, and provide academic leadership in teaching, research and other scholarly activities; (f) carry out academic and administrative duties as required; and (g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a) have a PhD degree in Social Policy and Administration / Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy or other related disciplines; (b) have a solid academic background as well as research and teaching expertise in the Chinese Mainland’s technological development and its impact on social development worldwide, including social impacts of AI and emerging technology, tech-driven social innovation, digital governance, and China’s social development and role in a global context; (c) possess strong capabilities in one or more of the Department’s existing core domains, including (i) social policy and accountability, with a focus on social policy analysis, social planning, comparative social policy, and health/labour/welfare policy; (ii) innovation and social development, with a focus on social entrepreneurship, labour and migration, and land and environment; and (iii) health, culture, and society, with a focus on sociology/anthropology of health, digital and techno-culture, and regional/area studies; (d) have proven track records in teaching and research; (e) have demonstrated record for establishing significant externally funded research programmes; (f) have considerable experience in academic programme planning, management and curriculum development; (g) demonstrate potential for research excellence, with proven ability to publish in high-quality journals being an advantage; (h) be open to the use of e-learning and blended learning strategies in teaching and scholarship; and (i) have local and international connections in research and professional capacities. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 17 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260803001": {
      "title": "Job Application - Instructor (Temporary Appointment)",
      "description": "Job Application - Instructor (Temporary Appointment) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Mechanical Engineering Instructor (Temporary Appointment) (Ref. 260803001) [Appointment period: twelve months] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    engage in a full range of activities related to teaching and learning, including preparing and developing materials, designing teaching and assessment strategies, delivering teaching in settings appropriate for the objective of learning, interacting with and motivating students, and assessing the performance of and giving feedback to students; (b)    assist in the development of subject curriculum and overall teaching and learning approach as well as in subject administration as required; (c)    assist in the activities pertaining to programme management; (d)    engage in departmental academic and administrative duties; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a relevant master’s degree plus at least one year of post-qualification tertiary or senior secondary teaching experience, and/or relevant professional, practical, or industrial experience; (b)    demonstrated promise of a high level of competence in teaching and carrying out subject administration responsibilities (and potential for contributing to curriculum/pedagogy development, subject and programme management and/or professional service if applicable); (c)    an excellent command of both written and spoken English; and (d)    good communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 August 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260730013": {
      "title": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Nursing",
      "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Nursing Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Nursing Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Nursing (Ref. 260730013) Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders.  It ranks 18 th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2026).  The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community.  Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members.  We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) provide quality teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels and supervise student projects and theses; (b) conduct research that leads to publications in refereed journals and award of research grants; (c) engage in applied research, creative development and consultancy projects in relation to health care related activities; (d) contribute to the development of the School’s relevant research theme and participate in its activities; (e) contribute to departmental activities and management; (f) render professional service to the community and support activities that promote or foster links with the profession in the industry and/or in the community; and (g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Applicants for appointment at Professor level should enhance his/her own international academic impact, play an active role in international academic exchange, and engage in services that contribute to the development of the School. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) a PhD degree in Nursing or a relevant discipline with substantial years of relevant experience; (b) professional nursing qualifications; (c) a substantial record and reputation as an accomplished teacher with significant contribution to curriculum development / review or teaching and learning processes; (d) an established track record in research and scholarship, including refereed publications, external grants and postgraduate supervision; and (e) demonstrated academic management and leadership capabilities. Applicants for appointment at Professor level should demonstrate a strong background in research in one of the school research themes with an international academic profile.  They should also demonstrate excellent international reputation in research and possess an excellent record of academic leadership and research scholarship, both in terms of publications and funded research.  Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Associate Professor/Assistant Professor. The job duty requirements and expectation would be in line with the appointed grade. Preference will be given to those who are registrable with The Nursing Council of Hong Kong. Applicants are invited to contact Professor Janelle Yorke, Head of School of Nursing via email at janelle.yorke@polyu.edu.hk for further information. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor and Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 13 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 30 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724015": {
      "title": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Optometry Part-time Visiting Lecturer (several  posts) (Ref. 260724015) [Appointment period: tenable for 2026/2027 academic year] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties in the Master of Science in Vision Science and Innovation programme; and (b)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have a doctoral degree, or a relevant first degree plus a higher degree and/or professional qualification in a relevant discipline and not less than three years of post-qualification teaching/research/practical and/or industrial experience. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is from HK$900 to HK$1,000 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 31 July 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724014": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Sports Science",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Sports Science Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Biomedical Engineering Assistant Professor in Sports Science (Ref. 260724014) The Department of Biomedical Engineering (BME) is one of the five academic departments in the Faculty of Engineering, and it offers a full spectrum of BME programmes, from BSc, MSc to PhD. The team is the first group to offer Biomedical Engineering related undergraduate programme in Hong Kong, and has made great achievements in BME education, innovative research, and technology transfer. Currently BME has six thematic research areas, including Biomedical Imaging, Sensing, AI and Wearable Technology, Brain-Machine Interface and Neural Engineering, Molecular/Cellular Engineering and Biomaterials, Precision Diagnostics and Therapy, Prosthetics-Orthotics, Smart Ageing and Rehabilitation Engineering, and Sports Science and Technology. It aims to conduct cutting-edge research in these areas and nurture future leaders in prosthetics and orthotics, clinical engineering, medical instrumentation and sensors, and biological engineering by imparting interdisciplinary knowledge, innovative ideas, critical thinking and practical skills. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/bme for more information about the Unit. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and contribute to programme and curriculum development; (b)    initiate innovative research projects that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of external research grants; (c)    supervise student projects and theses; (d)    engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (e)    undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in relevant disciplines; (b)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c)    published world-leading research as a main author; (d)    good networking ability; and (e)    excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 7 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724013": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Brain Machine Interface",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Brain Machine Interface Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Biomedical Engineering Assistant Professor in Brain Machine Interface (Ref. 260724013) The Department of Biomedical Engineering (BME) is one of the five academic departments in the Faculty of Engineering, and it offers a full spectrum of BME programmes, from BSc, MSc to PhD. The team is the first group to offer Biomedical Engineering related undergraduate programme in Hong Kong, and has made great achievements in BME education, innovative research, and technology transfer. Currently BME has six thematic research areas, including Biomedical Imaging, Sensing, AI and Wearable Technology, Brain-Machine Interface and Neural Engineering, Molecular/Cellular Engineering and Biomaterials, Precision Diagnostics and Therapy, Prosthetics-Orthotics, Smart Ageing and Rehabilitation Engineering, and Sports Science and Technology. It aims to conduct cutting-edge research in these areas and nurture future leaders in prosthetics and orthotics, clinical engineering, medical instrumentation and sensors, and biological engineering by imparting interdisciplinary knowledge, innovative ideas, critical thinking and practical skills. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/bme for more information about the Unit. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and contribute to programme and curriculum development; (b)    initiate innovative research projects that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of external research grants; (c)    supervise student projects and theses; (d)    engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (e)    undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in relevant disciplines; (b)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c)    published world-leading research as a main author; (d)    good networking ability; and (e)    excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 7 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
