    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724007": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Satellite and Space Engineering",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Satellite and Space Engineering Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering Assistant Professor in Satellite and Space Engineering (Ref. 260724007) In line with the strategic development of the University and to lead the development of the aeronautical and aviation engineering discipline in teaching and research activities, the Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering was established in the Faculty of Engineering. The Department currently offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and actively engages in various research and consultancy work. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/aae/ for more information about the Department.  Applications are now invited from academics who are actively involved in Satellite and Space Engineering to fill the vacancy for academic staff. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in his/her areas of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (b)    conduct research in satellite and space engineering and contribute to the development of the Department’s research strengths; (c)    supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (d)    undertake teaching duties at various levels in the area of satellite and space engineering; (e)    engage in programme/curriculum planning, development and administration; (f)     undertake relevant administrative duties; and (g)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Engineering with expertise in satellite and space engineering, including but not limited to spacecraft dynamics and control, payload and instrumentation, space robots, spacecraft design and tests, space technology applications such as navigation, remote sensing, and communications; (b)    experience in acquiring external research funding including national and international funding bodies and industries; (c)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (d)    effective classroom teaching skills and good interpersonal skills; and (e)    excellent communication, organisational and leadership skills, as well as strong cooperation skills with the ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724006": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Low-Altitude Economy",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Low-Altitude Economy Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering Assistant Professor in Low-Altitude Economy (Ref. 260724006) In line with the strategic development of the University and to lead the development of the aeronautical and aviation engineering discipline in teaching and research activities, the Department of Aeronautical and Aviation Engineering was established in the Faculty of Engineering. The Department currently offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and actively engages in various research and consultancy work. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/aae/ for more information about the Department.  Applications are now invited from academics who are actively involved in Low-Altitude Economy to fill the vacancy for academic staff. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in his/her areas of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (b)    conduct research in low-altitude economy and contribute to the development of the Department’s research strengths; (c)    supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (d)    undertake teaching duties at various levels in the area of low-altitude economy; (e)    engage in programme/curriculum planning, development and administration; (f)     undertake relevant administrative duties; and (g)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Engineering with expertise in low-altitude economy, including but not limited to unmanned aerial vehicles, advanced air mobility, perception, autonomous control, decision making, unmanned air traffic management, and applications (e.g. transportation, inspection, search and rescue, etc.); (b)    experience in acquiring external research funding including national and international funding bodies and industries; (c)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (d)    effective classroom teaching skills and good interpersonal skills; and (e)    excellent communication, organisational and leadership skills, as well as strong cooperation skills with the ability to work in an interdisciplinary team. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260724002": {
      "title": "Job Application - Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Job Application - Clinical Instructor Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Nursing Clinical Instructor (Ref. 260724002) Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders.  It ranks 18th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2026).  The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community.  Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members.  We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    supervise clinical projects and clinical practicum at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b)    teach pre-registration nursing programmes and supervise students in clinical/field studies; (c)    coordinate student clinical placement with local, national and overseas healthcare agencies; (d)    act as student advisor and counsellor; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a relevant master’s degree plus not less than three years of post-qualification/post-registration clinical experience in local hospitals; (b)    a Certificate of Registration (Part I and/or II) issued by The Nursing Board/Council of Hong Kong; (c)    a valid practising certificate issued by The Nursing Council of Hong Kong; and (d)    a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 7 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 24 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260715008": {
      "title": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer",
      "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of English and Communication Part-time Visiting Lecturer (Ref. 260715008) [Appointment period: from September 2026 to January 2027] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)        teach subject(s) for the BA (Hons) in English and Applied Linguistics programme; and (b)        perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a doctoral degree in Applied Linguistics, Communication, Media Studies, Art History, Visual Arts or a related discipline with at least three years of post-qualification teaching experience; (b)    a good command of written and spoken English; and (c)    good communication skills. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$950 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 28 July 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 15 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260713005": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Optimization and Operations Research / Statistics and Data Science/ Financial Mathematics / Engineering and Computational Mathematics / Mathematical Science / Actuarial Science",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Optimization and Operations Research / Statistics and Data Science/ Financial Mathematics / Engineering and Computational Mathematics / Mathematical Science / Actuarial Science Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Applied Mathematics Assistant Professor in Optimization and Operations Research / Statistics and Data Science/ Financial Mathematics / Engineering and Computational Mathematics / Mathematical Science / Actuarial Science (Ref. 260713005) The Department of Applied Mathematics (AMA) is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Computer and Mathematical Sciences.  Apart from making a significant contribution to most of other academic programmes of the University by providing service teaching, the Department also offers master programmes in Applied Mathematics for Science and Technology, Operational Research and Risk Analysis and Quantitative Finance and FinTech.  Starting from 2025/26 academic year, the Department offers a new Bachelor Scheme in Applied Mathematics and Finance Analytics and Fast-track Integrated Bachelor’s and Master’s Degree Programmes and will launch a new master programme, MSc in Mathematics for Artificial Intelligence Technology in 2026/27.  Members of the Department have expertise in applied optimization and optimal control, engineering computation, operational research, management science and applied statistics, FinTech, data science and machine learning.  There are currently 56 academic staff and about 154 research personnel in the Department.  Please visit the website at http://www.polyu.edu.hk/ama for more information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    teach and contribute to curriculum development at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b)    supervise MPhil and PhD students; (c)    engage in scholarly research, consultancy and other scholarly activities leading to publications in top-tier refereed journals and award of research grants; (d)    undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Department or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a PhD degree in Mathematics / Statistics / Financial Mathematics / Operations Research / Computational Mathematics / Applied Mathematics or a closely related field with experience in Data Science and Analytics; (b)    have expertise in applied statistics, operation research or mathematics; (c)    have an established track record in research and scholarship, including refereed publications and external grant applications; (d)    have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching; and (e)    be highly proficient in written and spoken English. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 10 August 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 13 July 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260624007": {
      "title": "Job Application - Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) in Building Environment",
      "description": "Job Application - Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) in Building Environment Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering Visiting Lecturer (Part-time) in Building Environment (Ref. 260624007) [Appointment period: from September 2026 to May 2027] The Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering (BEEE) contributes to PolyU’s world ranking of 21st for Architecture and Built Environment and 18th for Civil and Structural Engineering in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2026. BEEE is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Construction and Environment, and offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Philosophy, Master of Engineering, Master of Science and Bachelor of Engineering. Currently there are over 35 research staff and 190 research students (over 180 studying for PhD), over 600 full-time / part-time Master’s students, an undergraduate student body of over 250 full-time students.  BEEE currently has over 50 full-time academic / teaching staff members engaging in a wide range of research activities organised in the following three themes: Building Energy : Energy issues in buildings addressed in the context of both demand and supply to promote sustainable built environments, urban energy systems and emerging clean energy technologies. Building Environment : Optimisation of buildings and built environments for thermal comfort, indoor air quality, visual / spatial and vibration / acoustic aspects to improve occupant health and productivity, and extraterrestrial human habitats. Building Safety and Resilience : Protection of building occupants from hazards such as fire and lightning to improve safety and resilience of communities, buildings and the built environments. The University and the Department strongly encourage a multi-cultural environment regarding both the staff and student body composition. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/beee/ for further information about the Department. Duties The appointee will be required to teach and conduct assessments in the daytime course “ Water System Engineering in Built Environments (BSE4312) ” to undergraduate students in Semester 2 of the 2026/2027 academic year. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree OR a master’s degree in a related discipline with corporate membership in relevant professional bodies such as HKIE, CIBSE or CIPHE; (b)    at least three years of post-qualification teaching / practical training experience in a related discipline; and (c)    a good command of written and spoken English, and strong communication skills. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$900 per hour. C onsideration of applications will commence on 8 July 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260616018": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Design Teaching Fellow (Ref. 260616018) [Appointment period: twelve months] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    assist in the development of new subjects for the Service Design programme, including contributing to the design of course content and assessments; (b)    collaborate with the academic team to ensure the curriculum aligns with industry standards and emerging trends in service design, customer experience (CX) and strategic design; (c)    provide input and insights based on expertise in service design methodologies to enhance the quality and relevance of the programme content; (d)    work closely with the programme coordinator and faculty members to facilitate a smooth transition into the new programme as well as offering support in various administrative and educational tasks; (e)    support in the preparation and coordination of the admission exercise for the Service Design programme, including reviewing applications, conducting interviews, and evaluating portfolios; (f)     engage with prospective students to provide information about the programme, answer inquiries and assist with the admissions process; (g)    contribute to the planning and execution of promotional events and activities related to the Service Design programme; and (h)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a master’s degree in a relevant field related to service design, strategic design, user experience (UX)/CX design, or human-centered design plus not less than five years of post-qualification experience in tertiary teaching and/or professional practice within the service design industry or innovation consulting; (b)    demonstrate expertise and proficiency in the following areas essential to service design: •    proficiency in service design tools and frameworks (e.g. customer journey mapping, service blueprinting, stakeholder mapping and persona development); •    experience in both qualitative and quantitative design research methods (e.g. ethnographic research, in-depth interviews, co-creation workshops and usability testing); •    knowledge of systems thinking and organisational design; •    ability to design omni-channel service experiences by combining physical and digital touchpoints; •    expertise in facilitating participatory design and co-design sessions with diverse stakeholders; and •    proficiency in collaborative design and prototyping software (e.g. Figma, Miro, Mural, and Adobe Creative Cloud) tailored for service concept visualisation and prototyping. (c)    showcase the capacity to conduct tutorials, workshops and assessments within the service design and design thinking domain; (d)    demonstrate a keen ability to develop curriculum and convert materials to suit the unique requirements of service design and strategic innovation education; and (e)    possess exceptional oral and written communication skills as well as the ability to effectively engage with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 30 June 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 16 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260616011": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Division of Artificial Intelligence and the Humanities Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment) (Ref. 260616011) [Appointment period: twelve months initially, with possibility of further appointment] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties for the MSc in Generative AI and the Humanities programme, including the coordination and supervision of student seminars, tutorials and capstone projects/dissertation; (b)    engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (c)    contribute to the planning, administration and development of programmes/courses; (d)    assist in organising student activities/training workshops to enhance students’ learning experience; (e)    undertake administrative duties in academic and departmental affairs; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Division or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Computer Science or related disciplines; (b)    at least three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience and/or relevant professional, practical or industrial experience; (c)    good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the discipline; (d)    effective classroom teaching skills and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and professional service; (e)    an excellent command of both written and spoken English; and (f)     good communication and interpersonal skills. Applicants should also submit (i) an updated curriculum vitae; and (ii) a teaching statement elaborating his/her teaching philosophy and contribution for the position applied. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 2 July 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 16 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260608005": {
      "title": "Job Application - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Building Energy / Building Environment / Building Safety and Resilience under Strategic Hiring Scheme",
      "description": "Job Application - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Building Energy / Building Environment / Building Safety and Resilience under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Building Energy / Building Environment / Building Safety and Resilience under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 260608005) The Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering (BEEE) contributes to PolyU’s world ranking of 17th for Architecture and Built Environment as well as Civil and Structural Engineering in the QS World University Rankings by Subject 2025. BEEE is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Construction and Environment, and offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Philosophy, Master of Engineering, Master of Science and Bachelor of Engineering. Currently there are over 35 research staff and 201 research students (187 studying for PhD), over 600 full-time / part-time Master’s students, an undergraduate student body of over 250 full-time students.  BEEE currently has over 50 full-time academic / teaching staff members engaging in a wide range of research activities organised in the following three themes: Building Energy : Energy issues in buildings addressed in the context of both demand and supply to promote sustainable built environments, urban energy systems and emerging clean energy technologies. Building Environment : Optimisation of buildings and built environments for thermal comfort, indoor air quality, visual / spatial and vibration / acoustic aspects to improve occupant health and productivity, and Extraterrestrial human habitats. Building Safety and Resilience : Protection of building occupants from hazards such as fire and lightning to improve safety and resilience of communities, buildings and the built environments. The University and the Department strongly encourage a multi-cultural environment regarding both the staff and student body composition. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/beee/ for further information about the Department. BEEE is seeking internationally excellent candidate with exceptional track record of research and scholarship in the theme of Building Energy with preference to candidate demonstrating a strong and individualistic vision of the challenges facing modern urban environments and the opportunities afforded by emerging technologies to address them. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU’s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.  Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties at various levels; (b)    supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (c)    conduct research in related areas and contribute to the development of the Department’s research strength; (d)    initiate, lead and participate in scholarly research in his/her area of expertise and be active in research leading to quality journal publications and in bidding for external research grants and applied research projects; (e)    engage in programme / curriculum planning, administration and development; (f)     provide leadership in developing a programme, a subject discipline or a research programme, etc.; (g)    undertake relevant administrative duties; and (h)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a PhD degree in an appropriate related discipline; (b)    have strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c)    be able to demonstrate effective classroom teaching skills and have good interpersonal skills; (d)    have an excellent command of English; (e)    have an excellent record of research and scholarship commensurate with their experience; and (f)     demonstrate good potential in bidding for research grants as well as in establishing significant externally funded research programmes. The applicants should demonstrate strong potential to be internationally prominent through a track record of excellent research and teaching. They will be expected to contribute to the development and delivery of degree programmes; teach in engineering design relevant to their technical specialisation; and should have been involved in major research projects relevant to their discipline. Application is open to anyone with an outstanding research and teaching track record in the areas of Building Energy , Building Environment or Building Safety and Resilience . Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor level.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 22 June 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 8 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260603011": {
      "title": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer  (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Lecturer  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Optometry Part-time Visiting Lecturer  (several  posts) (Ref. 260603011) [Appointment period: tenable for 2026/2027 academic year] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    conduct teaching at undergraduate level in Optometry; and (b)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have a doctoral degree in Optometry or an equivalent qualification and not less than three years of post-qualification teaching experience. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is HK$900 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 17 June 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260603010": {
      "title": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Clinical Associate  (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Part-time Visiting Clinical Associate  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Optometry Part-time Visiting Clinical Associate  (several  posts) (Ref. 260603010) [Appointment period: tenable for 2026/2027 academic year] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    teach and supervise optometry students in their clinical training; and (b)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (c)    have a higher degree in Optometry or an equivalent qualification; (d)    have several years of relevant optometric experience; and (e)    be registered with the Optometrists Board of the HKSAR. Applicants possessing a bachelor’s degree in Optometry with substantial relevant industry and optometric experience may also be considered. Conditions of Service The remuneration rate is from HK$525 per hour. Consideration of applications will commence on 17 June 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 3 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260601010": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Biomedical Engineering Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Biomedical Engineering Assistant Professor in Biomedical Engineering (Ref. 260601010) The Department of Biomedical Engineering (BME) is one of the five academic departments in the Faculty of Engineering, and it offers a full spectrum of BME programmes, from BSc, MSc to PhD.  The team is the first group to offer Biomedical Engineering related undergraduate programme in Hong Kong, and has made great achievements in BME education, innovative research, and technology transfer.  Currently BME has four thematic research areas, including Biomedical Imaging, Instrumentation, Sensing and AI, Molecular, Cellular and Tissue Engineering, Sports and Neuromusculoskeletal Engineering, Prosthetics, Orthotics, Smart Ageing and Rehabilitation Engineering.  It aims to conduct cutting-edge researches in these areas and nurture future leaders in prosthetics and orthotics, clinical engineering, medical instrumentation and sensors, and biological engineering by imparting interdisciplinary knowledge, innovative ideas, critical thinking and practical skills.  Please visit the website at http://www.polyu.edu.hk/bme for more information about the Unit. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and contribute to programme and curriculum development; (b)    initiate innovative research projects that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of external research grants; (c)    supervise student projects and theses; (d)    engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (e)    undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Biomedical Engineering or Neurotechnology, with expertise in Biomedical Imaging or Brain Computer Interface or a related discipline; (b)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c)    good publication records; (d)    good networking ability; and (e)    excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Appointment will only be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract. Consideration of applications will commence on 15 June 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 1 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260601004": {
      "title": "Job Application - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Design",
      "description": "Job Application - Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Design Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Design Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Design (Ref. 260601004) The School of Design, a leading and transdisciplinary design school, is at the forefront of nurturing capable, open-minded, creative talents and active learners; contributing to innovation in Hong Kong and the Chinese Mainland while maintaining a global perspective.  As one of the top design schools in the world, its highly diverse design expertise widely covers Product Design, Interaction Design, Information Design, Advertising Design, Media Design, Interior Design, Environmental Design, Social Design, Service Design, Transitional Environments Design, Innovative Business Design, Intelligent Systems Design, Smart Service Design and Innovative Multimedia Entertainment.  It is consistently ranked among the top 25 on the Quacquarelli Symonds (QS) World University Rankings by Subject - Art and Design.  The School is based in a Zaha Hadid designed building well-equipped for innovative research and creative learning on the university campus.  Please visit the website at https://www.sd.polyu.edu.hk/en/ for more information about the School. The School attaches equal importance to design theory and application, integrates art with science, actively promotes interdisciplinary cooperation and learning, emphasises high-quality design education, conducts high-level research, and provides consulting services. The School is committed to contributing its expertise to the community through applied research and consultancy, providing forward-looking advice and support to the industry covering three main pillars: Design Intelligence, Design for Virtue, and Design Wellbeings; and contributes to innovation in Hong Kong and the Chinese Mainland, while maintaining a global perspective. The School is looking for candidates who will work in a transdisciplinary design environment that builds on the School’s global position within the regional and Chinese context (e.g. the Greater Bay Area). More specifically, candidates are sought, preferably with industry experience together with a strong track record of teaching and research in any one of the following areas: Communication Design (e.g. strategy, branding, creative advertising, market research, content creation, information design, infographics, wayfinding, animation content creation, filmmaking, storytelling) Content Design (e.g. digital content creation, digital communication design, brand development, publication design) Design for Entrepreneurship (e.g. design strategy, user-centered design, design management, circular design, product service systems) Digital Entertainment and Game Development (e.g. applied anthropology, psychology, neuroscience, socio-technical systems) Interactive System Design (e.g. UX design, smart product, design for AI, internet of things, digital fabrication, data driven design) Service Design and Social Innovation (e.g. strategic innovation, user experience design, organisational/community design) Interaction Design (e.g., design-oriented HCI, user experience and interface design, research through design, design methodologies, interactive computing) Candidates are expected to demonstrate a strong research potential and/or good publication track record in transdisciplinary design projects (e.g. healthcare systems, smart tourism, e-enterprises, city-regeneration, age-friendly city, etc.). Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    synthesise knowledge and design applications with theories, design research methods and form-giving techniques; (b)    provide leadership in all aspects of academic activities, including research, teaching and service among the design disciplines; (c)    teach at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels in a mix of design disciplines; (d)    act as student advisor and supervisor to groups as well as individual students including research students; (e)    secure competitive research grants and conduct research that leads to publications in refereed journals, or a body of design work which leads to outputs contributing to the knowledge and teaching of the design disciplines; (f)    engage actively in research and scholarly activities serving the regional and international industry with significance and relevance to the discipline and profession; (g)    work with industry, nonprofits and the public sector to initiate funded research projects; (h)    activate inter-departmental and inter-institutional collaboration and networking; and (i)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a relevant PhD degree with professional and/or teaching experiences in a specialised area of design and/or a related discipline; (b)    extensive knowledge of and expertise in an area of design with hands-on techniques; (c)    extensive knowledge of and track record in design research and research methodologies; (d)    a high level of contextual and cultural awareness, and a vision for the future development of the profession; and (e)    a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, research and professional service. Applicants for appointment at Associate Professor level should have stronger relevant academic and/or professional achievements. Candidates with less experience will be considered for appointment at a lower level. Applicant should submit (a) a letter of application declaring a focus area of expertise; (b) updated curriculum vitae; (c) a brief statement of research and teaching philosophy; (d) three key publications; and (e) a design and/or teaching portfolio including samples of personal and professional work. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor level.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 31 July 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 1 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260521007": {
      "title": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Microelectronics and Quantum Technology under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Microelectronics and Quantum Technology under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Microelectronics and Quantum Technology under Strategic Hiring Scheme  (several  posts) (Ref. 260521007) Since its inception in 1974, the Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering (EEE), formed through the merger of the Department of Electronic and Information Engineering and the Department of Electrical Engineering, has maintained a distinguished history of providing outstanding engineering education and applied research in Hong Kong. The Unit offers extensive resources to support a wide variety of teaching activities and research interests, frequently hosting leading scholars for collaboration to enhance its global research profile. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/eee for more information about the Unit. EEE is a constituent unit in the Faculty of Engineering. Information on the Faculty is available at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/feng/ . To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU’s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.  Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. EEE is now seeking highly qualified candidates for Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor positions across several strategic research tracks. Duties (A) Microelectronics and Silicon Photonics Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in devices design, cleanroom fabrication and device characterization etc. EEE prioritizes expertise in device design, simulation, fabrication and packaging, specifically encouraging those with experience bridging microelectronics with silicon photonics or heterogeneous integration. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on silicon photonics and microelectronics. (B) Embedded Circuits and Packaging Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in advanced embedded circuits and electronic packaging technologies. EEE prioritizes expertise in embedded circuit design, simulation and system-level integration, specifically encouraging those with experience in SoC architectures, 2.5D/3D integration, chiplet packaging or co-packaged optics with FPGA. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on embedded circuit design and advanced packaging technologies. (C) Photonic Quantum Computing Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in quantum optics, integrated quantum photonics and photonic quantum computing experiments. EEE prioritizes expertise in quantum light sources and programmable photonic circuits, specifically encouraging those with experience in optical quantum information processing or hardware implementation of quantum algorithms. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on quantum optics, quantum computing, and quantum information processing. (D) Quantum Theory and Algorithms Appointees for this track should possess substantial research experience in quantum optics, photonic quantum computing theory, architectures and quantum error correction. EEE prioritizes expertise in developing architectures for scalable photonic quantum computers and designing quantum machine learning models, specifically encouraging those with experience in practical quantum applications or collaborating closely with experimental teams. Teaching Duties: The appointees will be responsible for delivering courses at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels specifically focused on quantum algorithms and quantum information theory. For all the above tracks, the appointees will also be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in the area of Microelectronics, Photonics, Quantum Physics or Quantum Technology. Beyond these primary areas, the candidate should be prepared to contribute to multidisciplinary subjects across the EEE curriculum; (b)    conduct research that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; (c)    attract research fundings and support industrial researches; (d)    supervise student projects and theses; (e)    engage in scholarly research/consultancy in their area of expertise; (f)     contribute to departmental services and activities; and (g)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline; (b)    have the relevant postdoctoral research experience and a publication record that is commensurate with the level of appointment; (c)    demonstrate excellence in original research and strong fundamental knowledge in one or more of the above-mentioned core research areas; (d)    demonstrate potential to establish significant externally funded research programmes; (e)    be able to demonstrate evidence of effective classroom teaching skills; and (f)     have excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Professor / Associate Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 28 May 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 21 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260513001": {
      "title": "Post Specification",
      "description": "Job Application - Joseph Needham Professorship in Science and Civilisation Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Faculty of Humanities Joseph Needham Professorship in Science and Civilisation (Ref. 260513001) The Faculty of Humanities at The Hong Kong Polytechnic University is dedicated to creating synergies among language, communication, history, culture, and technology in education and research, highlighting both the discovery and the transfer of knowledge.  It is a leading tertiary education provider in Asia in the fields of linguistics, language science, language technology, Chinese-English bilingual studies and translation, intercultural communication, professional communication, and cultural and historical studies of China. The Faculty also excels in areas such as AI and the humanities, computational linguistics, healthcare communication, language neuroscience, sociolinguistic studies, and speech therapy.  It consists of four academic units: Department of Chinese History and Culture, Department of English and Communication, Department of Language Science and Technology, and Division of Artificial Intelligence and the Humanities.  The appointee will be appointed as Chair Professor / Professor in one of the academic units under the Faculty of Humanities.  Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/fh for more information about the Faculty. Duties The position calls for a visionary academic leader to advance the strategic and sustainable development of the Faculty in Science and Civilisation. The successful candidate will combine world-class scholarship with exceptional leadership to shape the future of these disciplines. The appointee will be required to: (a)    provide leadership in long-term strategic planning that aligns with the University’s goals; (b)    provide leadership in strengthening local and international partnerships to advance research and education goals; (c)    develop scholarly initiatives by fostering collaboration, securing external funding, and enhancing innovative, high-impact interdisciplinary research; (d)    mentor junior faculty in teaching, research and service excellence; (e)    teach and develop curricula in science and civilisation, including Chinese science and technology history, at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (f)     supervise postgraduate students actively and provide guidance on their research and career development; (g)    provide active service to committee work at all levels in the Faculty and the University as well as to the scholarly community; (h)    provide administrative support and advice for academic and Faculty/department affairs; and (i)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in a relevant discipline, evidence of eminent scholarship and substantial relevant experience in a senior academic position, and relevant professional qualifications where appropriate; (b)    a global perspective, proven track record of academic leadership, and a distinguished international reputation in research and scholarship; (c)    a strong record in attracting and managing competitive research funding; (d)    a strong potential to develop local and international networks of partnerships and linkages with the community, for both professional and public sectors; (e)    a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning with substantial relevant teaching experiences; (f)     proven academic leadership and ability to foster collaboration with colleagues in teaching, intellectual contributions, and service activities to bring visibility, prestige and reputation to the University; and (g)    an excellent command of both English and Chinese. Applicants for appointment at the Chair Professor level should have attainment of an academic rank of full professor or above at an internationally reputable university. Applicants for appointment at the Professor level should have an excellent international reputation as a leading scholar. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement need not re-apply. Conditions of Service Terms of appointment and remuneration package are negotiable and highly competitive. For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Application and Nomination The University invites applications and nominations for this appointment.  Please submit an application by clicking the “Apply Now” button below.  Candidature may also be recommended by nominations via email to fh.search@polyu.edu.hk .  General information about the University is available at https://www.polyu.edu.hk or from the Human Resources Office [Tel: (852) 2766 5291]. Consideration of applications and nominations will commence on 1 July 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 13 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512006": {
      "title": "Job Application - Instructor (English Language)  (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Instructor (English Language)  (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Instructor (English Language)  (several  posts) (Ref. 260512006) The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.  It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.  CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students’ language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life‑long learning, and support whole‑person development.  They provide English and Chinese language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University’s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements.  In addition to curriculum‑based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co‑curricular learning activities to support students’ academic development and learning needs.  Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)     teach a range of courses in English for Academic Purposes (EAP), English for Specific Purposes (ESP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b)     engage in English language enhancement initiatives of the University, including workshops and support activities related to technology- and AI-enhanced language learning; (c)     participate in the pedagogical development and administration of teaching and learning activities, including promoting student language skills through technology-enhanced language teaching methods and responsible AI use; and (d)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a master’s degree in English Language Education / TESOL / Applied Linguistics / Education or a related discipline; (b)    have a recognised language teaching qualification; (c)    preferably possess at least three years’ post-qualification relevant teaching experience at tertiary level; (d)    have effective classroom teaching skills; (e)    have demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (f)     have demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for English language education; and (g)    be a highly proficient English speaker. Preference will be given to teachers with experience or expertise in incorporating GenAI in language teaching, expertise in discipline-related English, digital literacies, assessment design, and supporting students to use AI tools for self-regulated language learning. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1 June 2026 . Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512005": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several  posts) (Ref. 260512005) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.  It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.  CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students’ language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life‑long learning, and support whole‑person development.  They provide English and Chinese language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University’s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements.  In addition to curriculum‑based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co‑curricular learning activities to support students’ academic development and learning needs.  Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    teach a range of courses in English for Academic Purposes (EAP), English for Specific Purposes (ESP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b)    teach and lead curriculum development in English language education, including AI-integrated syllabus/assessment design and student guidance on responsible AI use; (c)    make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the English Language Centre’s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; and (d)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a master’s degree in English Language Education / TESOL / Applied Linguistics / Education or a related discipline; (b)    have a recognised language teaching qualification; (c)    possess at least four years’ relevant post-qualification experience at tertiary level, with a good track record of teaching English in higher education; (d)    have experience in course and instructional design, including technology-enhanced learning; (e)    have demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (f)     have demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for English language education; and (g)    be a highly proficient English speaker. Applicants should be active members within the discipline of language education as evidenced through participation in relevant conferences, the production of language teaching materials, and/or instructional design.  Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in EAP/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1 June 2026 . Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512004": {
      "title": "Job Application - Senior Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Senior Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Senior Teaching Fellow (English Language) (several posts) (Ref. 260512004) [will be conferred the title of Senior Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.  It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.  CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students’ language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life‑long learning, and support whole‑person development.  They provide English and Chinese language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University’s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements.  In addition to curriculum‑based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co‑curricular learning activities to support students’ academic development and learning needs.  Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    teach a range of courses in English for Academic Purposes (EAP), English for Specific Purposes (ESP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b)    provide effective and visionary leadership in a position of responsibility as coordinator of at least one major aspect of the English Language Centre’s operation, including (where appropriate) leadership in AI-integrated curriculum, assessment and responsible-use practices; (c)    make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the Centre’s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; (d)    play a leading administrative and pedagogic role in the Centre’s operation, including mentoring colleagues in AI-enhanced language teaching and the development of student AI literacy; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a master’s degree in English Language Education / TESOL / Applied Linguistics / Education or a related discipline, and preferably a PhD in a relevant field; (b)    a recognised language teaching qualification; (c)    at least nine years’ post-master’s or at least six years’ post-doctoral relevant teaching experience at tertiary level, with a strong track record of teaching English in higher education; (d)    considerable experience of, and demonstrated competence in, the coordination and management of teaching and learning activity at tertiary level, including curriculum leadership and quality assurance; (e)    demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (f)     demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for English language education; and (g)    a high proficiency in spoken and written English. Applicants should demonstrate active scholarly engagement in the field of language education, through activities such as leading teaching-related projects, delivering presentations and publishing research at relevant conferences, developing language teaching materials, and/or undertaking instructional design work.  Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in EAP/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1 June 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512003": {
      "title": "Job Application - Instructor (Chinese Language) (several posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Instructor (Chinese Language) (several posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Instructor (Chinese Language) (several posts) (Ref. 260512003) The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.  It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.  CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students’ language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life‑long learning, and support whole‑person development.  They provide Chinese and English language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University’s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements.  In addition to curriculum‑based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co‑curricular learning activities to support students’ academic development and learning needs.  Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    teach a range of courses in Chinese for Academic Purposes (CAP), Chinese for Specific Purposes (CSP) and communication skills for undergraduate students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b)    engage in Chinese language enhancement initiatives of the University, including workshops and support activities related to technology- and AI-enhanced language learning; (c)    participate in the pedagogical development and administration of teaching and learning activities, including promoting student language skills through technology-enhanced language teaching methods and responsible AI use; and (d)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a master’s degree in Applied Linguistics / Chinese Language/Literature / Chinese Language Education or a related discipline; (b)    preferably at least three years’ post-qualification relevant teaching experience at tertiary level; (c)    effective classroom teaching skills; (d)    demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (e)    demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for Chinese language education; (f)     an excellent command of written Chinese with proficiency in Putonghua (at least B2 level in Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi [PSC] or equivalent) and Cantonese; and (g)    the ability to use English as a working language. Preference will be given to teachers with experience or expertise in incorporating GenAI in language teaching, expertise in discipline-related Chinese, digital literacies, assessment design, and supporting students to use AI tools for self-regulated language learning. Preference may be given to those with relevant teaching experience in Chinese/Putonghua at tertiary level, including subjects offered to non-Chinese speaking students. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 1 June 2026 . Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512002": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) (Ref. 260512002) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.  It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.  CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students’ language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life‑long learning, and support whole‑person development.  They provide Chinese and English language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University’s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements.  In addition to curriculum‑based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co‑curricular learning activities to support students’ academic development and learning needs.  Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    teach a range of courses in Chinese for Academic Purposes (CAP), Chinese for Specific Purposes (CSP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b)    teach and lead curriculum development in Chinese language education, including AI-integrated syllabus/assessment design and student guidance on responsible AI use; (c)    make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the Chinese Language Centre’s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; and (d)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a master’s degree in Applied Linguistics / Chinese Language/Literature / Language Education or a related discipline; (b)    at least four years’ relevant post-qualification experience at tertiary level, with a good track record of teaching Chinese in higher education; (c)    experience in course and instructional design, including technology-enhanced learning; (d)    demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (e)    demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for Chinese language education; (f)     an excellent command of written Chinese with proficiency in Putonghua (at least B2 level in Putonghua Shuiping Ceshi [PSC] or equivalent) and Cantonese; and (g)    the ability to use English as a working language. Applicants should be active members within the discipline of language education as evidenced through participation in relevant conferences, the production of language teaching materials, and/or instructional design.  Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in Chinese for Academic Purpose/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1 June 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260512001": {
      "title": "Job Application - Senior Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Senior Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Language Education Institute Senior Teaching Fellow (Chinese Language) (several  posts) (Ref. 260512001) [will be conferred the title of Senior Lecturer] The Language Education Institute (LEI), a new academic unit established on 1 July 2025, formulates policies, designs curricula and delivers teaching activities for the education of languages among students at PolyU, focusing mainly on the Chinese and English languages. LEI strives to become a regional and international leader in language education, particularly in the application of the latest technologies in language learning, teaching and assessment.  It drives scholarship and best practices in language education among the PolyU community. LEI comprises the Chinese Language Centre (CLC), English Language Centre (ELC) and Technology-Enhanced Language Education Centre (TELEC), which are constituent units with their own Directors.  CLC and ELC offer service language teaching in Chinese and English for all students in the University while TELEC undertakes service language teaching using digital learning platforms and technological tools such as artificial intelligence and immersive technologies. CLC and ELC are committed to excellence in learning and teaching and aim to strengthen students’ language proficiency and communication skills, foster independent and life‑long learning, and support whole‑person development.  They provide Chinese and English language teaching services tailored to the diverse needs of the University’s students, delivering language enhancement and communication subjects, including AI as a Tool for Language Learning, in accordance with University requirements.  In addition to curriculum‑based teaching, the Centres coordinate a range of co‑curricular learning activities to support students’ academic development and learning needs.  Please visit the websites at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/clc/ and https://www.polyu.edu.hk/elc/ respectively for more information about CLC and ELC. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    teach a range of courses in Chinese for Academic Purposes (CAP), Chinese for Specific Purposes (CSP) and communication skills for students, with effective and responsible integration of AI/GenAI to enhance learning, teaching, and assessment; (b)    provide effective and visionary leadership in a position of responsibility as coordinator of at least one major aspect of the Chinese Language Centre’s operation, including (where appropriate) leadership in AI-integrated curriculum, assessment and responsible-use practices; (c)    make a considerable contribution to the various aspects of the Centre’s work and digital initiatives through committee membership; (d)    play a leading administrative and pedagogic role in the Centre’s operation, including mentoring colleagues in AI-enhanced language teaching and the development of student AI literacy; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Director of Language Education Institute or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a master’s degree in Applied Linguistics / Chinese Language/Literature / Language Education or a related discipline, and preferably a PhD in a relevant field; (b)    at least nine years’ post-Master’s or at least six years’ post-doctoral relevant teaching experience at tertiary level, with a strong track record of teaching Chinese in higher education; (c)    considerable experience of, and demonstrated competence in, the coordination and management of teaching and learning activities at tertiary level, including curriculum leadership and quality assurance; (d)    demonstrated strong commitment to excellence in teaching; (e)    demonstrated pedagogic AI competencies for Chinese language education; and (f)     the ability to use English as a working language. Applicants should demonstrate active scholarly engagement in the field of language education, through activities such as leading teaching-related projects, delivering presentations and publishing research at relevant conferences, developing language teaching materials, and/or undertaking instructional design work.  Applications are particularly welcome from teachers with expertise in Chinese for Academic Purpose/academic literacy, multimodal communication, instructional and curriculum design, AI/GenAI-enhanced language pedagogy, or other areas of Applied Linguistics if of direct relevance to Language Education. Applicants should indicate in their cover letter how their qualifications and experience would enable them to effectively perform the duties of the post. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 1 June 2026. Apply Now Posting date: 12 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260505010": {
      "title": "Job Application - Clinical Associate (two posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Clinical Associate (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Nursing Clinical Associate (two posts) (Ref. 260505010) [will be conferred the title of Assistant Professor of Practice] Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders.  It ranks 18th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2026).  The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community.  Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members.  We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a) perform classroom teaching and clinical supervision duties in nursing and related areas; (b) teach pre-registration nursing programmes and supervise students in clinical/field studies; (c) supervise clinical projects and clinical practicum at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (d) contribute to curriculum development and quality improvement of clinical studies; (e) act as student advisor and counsellor; (f)  coordinate student clinical placement with local, national and overseas healthcare agencies; and (g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) a relevant master’s degree plus not less than four years of post-qualification/post-registration clinical experience in nursing or related areas; (b) a Certificate of Registration (Part I and/or II) issued by The Nursing Board/Council of Hong Kong; (c) a valid practicing certificate issued by The Nursing Council of Hong Kong; (d) a solid track record as a nursing educator with demonstrated experience in both hands-on clinical supervision and classroom teaching; (e) significant contribution to educational innovations and quality improvement initiatives across both clinical practicum and academic settings; (f) demonstrated potential for making substantial contributions to curriculum and pedagogy development and programme management; (g) a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese; and (h) effective pedagogical skills across various delivery formats, including classroom teaching and direct clinical supervision, coupled with good interpersonal and communication skills. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 19 May 2026 until the positions are filled. Apply Now Posting date: 5 May 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260427004": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Shipping, Maritime and Transport Studies",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Shipping, Maritime and Transport Studies Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies Teaching Fellow in Shipping, Maritime and Transport Studies (Ref. 260427004) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    engage in teaching Logistics and Maritime Studies subjects and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b)    contribute to programme/curriculum design, development and administration, and engage actively in scholarly activities; (c)    provide support for academic and departmental affairs; and (d)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline plus not less than three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience; (b)    good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the appropriate academic or professional discipline; (c)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching; and (d)    an excellent command of English and good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with relevant teaching experience in tertiary institutions. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement(s) need not re-apply. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 11 June 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 4 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260424016": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)  (three posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)  (three posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Computing Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)  (three posts) (Ref. 260424016) [Appointment period: each for twelve months initially, with possibility of further appointment] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including the coordination and supervision of student seminars, tutorials and projects/theses; (b)    engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (c)    contribute to the planning, administration and development of programmes/courses; (d)    assist in organising student activities/training workshops to promote students’ learning experience; (e)    undertake administrative duties in academic and departmental affairs; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Computer Science, Information Technology or related disciplines; (b)    at least three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience and/or relevant professional, practical, or industrial experience; (c)    good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the discipline; (d)    effective classroom teaching skills and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and professional service; and (e)    an excellent command of both written and spoken English, good communication and interpersonal skills. Applicants should also submit (i) an updated curriculum vitae; and (ii) a teaching statement elaborating his/her teaching philosophy and contribution for the position applied. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. C onsideration of applications will commence on 15 May 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 April 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260421011": {
      "title": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Management",
      "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Management Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Management and Marketing Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Management (Ref. 260421011) The Department of Management and Marketing (MM) is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Business. According to the 2025 US News and World Report Global University Ranking, PolyU is ranked 58 th in the Best Global Universities and 25 th in the Best Universities for Economics and Business (7 th in Asia). The University of Texas at Dallas ranks our faculty's research 38 th in the world and 5 th in Asia (as of March 2026). MM currently has around 60 full-time academic staff who are dedicated to providing cutting-edge knowledge and practical skills for our students in three key areas of business — Management , Marketing , and Management Information Systems . We offer a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Science, and Bachelor of Business Administration. Our doctoral program has successfully placed our PhD students in elite institutions in Asia and Australia, including Hong Kong University of Science & Technology, City University of Hong Kong, Renmin University, and Deakin University. The Management discipline of the Department invites applications for open-ranked faculty positions in the Organisational Behavior and Human Resources (OBHR) and Strategic Management areas . The faculty members in the Management discipline of MM regularly publish their research in top-tier journals such as the Academy of Management Journal , Journal of Applied Psychology , Strategic Management Journal , Organization Science , Journal of International Business Studies , and other premier outlets. Our research support includes a reduced teaching load in the first three years, generous start-up grant, and considerate administrative services for junior members. The department has a collegial environment. Currently the OBHR team includes Wu Liu, Michael Bond, Krishna Savani, Yi (Amy) Ou, Jia (Katrina) Lin, Jun (Melody) Zhang, Ren Li, Mannok Wong, Zhishuang (Olivia) Guan, Jingfeng Yin, and Kun Wang; the Strategic Management team includes Chinien Chung, Shuping Li, Xueyong Zhan, Qi Zhu, Hangjun Cho, Junghyun Mah, and Qinyu (Ryan) Wang. Please visit the website at https://mm.polyu.edu.hk/ for more information about MM.  Applicants are invited to contact Professor Wu Liu, Professor of Department of Management and Marketing by email at wu.liu@polyu.edu.hk or Professor Chinien Chung, Associate Dean and Chair Professor of Strategic and Organization Management by email at chinien.chung@polyu.edu.hk for further information about the post. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    engage in top-level scholarly research in their areas of expertise; (b)    supervise research students; (c)    secure external competitive research grants; (d)    teach at the undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels; and (e)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Management or a relevant discipline at the time of appointment or be close to receiving it; and (b)    a focused research orientation and the potential or demonstrated ability to publish in high quality scholarly journals. Conditions of Service The compensation package, teaching loads, and research support are highly competitive.  Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . C onsideration of applications will commence on 2 July 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 24 June 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260421008": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Design Teaching Fellow (Ref. 260421008) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    develop subjects for the Social Design programme that synthesises knowledge and design applications with theories, design research methods and form-giving techniques; (b)    teach at the undergraduate level across all levels of the undergraduate Bachelor of Arts (BA) Design programme and across core and elective studio, seminar and lecture subjects, with adjustment in the teaching delivery to correspond to the subject; (c)    work closely with the programme coordinator and faculty members to facilitate the execution of the programme and offer support in various administrative and educational tasks, academic activities and service which may span design disciplines; (d)    support the preparation and coordination of the admission exercise for the Social and Service Design programme, which may include reviewing applications, conducting interviews, and evaluating portfolios; (e)    act as an academic advisor and provide student support across all student levels as needed with intensive supervisory support provided to final year students completing their final year project; (f)    collaborate with the academic team to ensure curriculum alignment with industry standards and emerging trends in social and service design, community engagement, and sustainable practices, with a view to programme relevance and institutional influence; (g)    provide insights and expertise in social design methodologies, community engagement strategies, and sustainable development to enhance programme content quality and relevance; (h)    engage with prospective students to provide information about the programme, answer inquiries, and assist in the admission process; (i)     contribute to the planning and execution of promotional events and activities related to the launch and continuing reputation of the Social and Service Design programme; (j)     actively seek out inter-departmental collaborative teaching opportunities that promote the BA Design Scheme as a whole; and (k)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a master’s degree in disciplines related to social design, service design, community development, or related fields, with not less than three years of post-qualification experience in tertiary teaching and/or professional practice within the social and service design industry; (b)    demonstrate expertise and proficiency in: •    procedural workflows in social and service design and utilisation of tools for designing interventions; •    community engagement strategies, including working with diverse communities and advocating for marginalised populations; and •    curriculum development tailored to the unique requirements of social and service design education; (c)    showcase the ability to conduct tutorials, workshops and assessments within the domain of social and service design; (d)    possess exceptional oral and written communication skills to effectively engage with individuals from diverse backgrounds; and (e)    be strongly committed to excellence in teaching and learning. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 28 April 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 21 April 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260415007": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Supply Chain and Operations Management  (two posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Supply Chain and Operations Management  (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Logistics and Maritime Studies Teaching Fellow in Supply Chain and Operations Management  (two posts) (Ref. 260415007) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    engage in teaching Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Operations and Quality Management related subjects and undertake related pedagogical activities at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (b)    contribute to programme/curriculum design, development and administration, and engage actively in scholarly activities; (c)    provide support for academic and departmental affairs; and (d)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Unit or his delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a doctoral degree in a relevant discipline plus not less than three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience; (b)    good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the appropriate academic or professional discipline; (c)    strong commitment to excellence in teaching; and (d)    an excellent command of English and good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with relevant teaching experience in tertiary institutions. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. C onsideration of applications will commence on 22 April 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 15 April 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260327018": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Construction and Real Estate Technology",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow in Construction and Real Estate Technology Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Construction Management and Intelligence Teaching Fellow in Construction and Real Estate Technology (Ref. 260327018) [will be conferred the title of Lecturer] The Department of Construction Management and Intelligence (retitled from the Department of Building and Real Estate in July 2026) is one of the constituent departments of the Faculty of Construction and Environment. The Department offers a full range of programmes leading to the awards of Doctor of Philosophy, Master of Philosophy, Master of Science and Bachelor of Science. It has an undergraduate student body of over 600 full-time students and a postgraduate student body of over 300. The Department currently has a total of 30 full-time academic / teaching staff, 20 technical and administrative staff and over 100 research personnel. The Department is committed to excellence in teaching, research and service to the community. Please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cmi/ for more information about the Department. The Department is looking for enthusiastic, established and suitably qualified person to join the Department to take part in a number of teaching and research activities. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    conduct lectures, tutorials and supervise students at undergraduate and/or postgraduate levels in construction technology, engineering management and related areas.   Some evening teaching is expected; (b)    prepare teaching materials including hand-outs, presentations, coursework assignments, examination papers, etc.; (c)    meet with students during office or assigned hours on academic matters, career issues and other appropriate matters; (d)    assess students’ study progress by periodic evaluations through coursework assignments, tests and examinations according to established grading scheme / policy; (e)    propose / plan new programmes, design / review subject / programme curriculum, and design / facilitate learning activities; (f)     contribute to subject / programme validation and coordinate programme quality assurance processes; (g)    help promote teaching quality by leading / organising teaching development projects, and/or chairing / serving on teaching-related committees / panels, and by means of workshops / forums and by coaching / mentoring other junior teaching staff to become better teachers; (h)    engage actively in scholarly activities; (i)     perform administrative duties as and when called upon by the Head of Unit; (j)     render professional service to the community and support activities that promote or foster links with the profession in the industry and/or in the community, e.g. serving on committees of external bodies of the profession, etc.; and (k)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a relevant master’s degree in Construction or a closely related field, plus not less than  three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience and/or relevant professional, practical or industrial experience; (b)    strong competencies in design and delivery of teaching, curriculum and pedagogy development, and subject administration; (c)    a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese; and (d)    good teamwork, communication and interpersonal skills. Preference will be given to those with programme management and leadership.  Holder of relevant professional qualification will be favourably considered. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement need not re-apply. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 15 April 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 27 March 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260326010": {
      "title": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Humanities  (two posts)",
      "description": "Job Application - Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Humanities  (two posts) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Division of Artificial Intelligence and the Humanities Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence and Humanities  (two posts) (Ref. 260326010) The Division of Artificial Intelligence and the Humanities (AIH), a constituent academic unit within the Faculty of Humanities, is dedicated to advancing innovation at the intersection of artificial intelligence and humanistic inquiry. Positioned at the forefront of emerging technologies, AIH aims to promote the development of human-centred AI that enhances society through ethical, creative, and interdisciplinary approaches. The Master of Science in Generative AI and the Humanities programme, launched in 2024 as the first-of-its-kind in Hong Kong and the world, serves as a flagship initiative of the Division. The programme is designed to equip students with a comprehensive understanding of AI’s impact on language, communication, the arts, and culture, and to prepare them for leadership in an AI-driven future. AIH invites applications for multiple faculty positions across all academic ranks, with a preference for appointments at the Assistant Professor level. We seek applicants who are committed to leading the integration of AI into humanities-focused education, research, and knowledge transfer. Areas of particular interest include language science and technology, neuroscience and health, language teaching and learning, and Chinese history and culture. Ideal candidates should possess strong programming skills and solid understanding of AI methodologies, along with a deep engagement with humanistic inquiry and its broader potential. The ability to work collaboratively across departments is essential. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties at the undergraduate and postgraduate levels, and contribute to programme and curriculum development; (b)    supervise students and their projects at the undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (c)    conduct research in related areas and contribute to the development of the AIH’s strategic research areas; (d)    initiate, lead, and participate in scholarly research in his/her area of expertise that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals and awards of external research grants; (e)    contribute to departmental service; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Division or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a PhD degree in relevant disciplines; (b)    demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (c)    have a proven track record in research and academic achievements; and (d)    be able to demonstrate effective classroom teaching skills, with the ability to use English as the medium of instruction. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 25 April 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 26 March 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260313002": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Design Teaching Fellow (Ref. 260313002) [Appointment period: twelve months] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    assist in the development of new subjects for the upcoming Media Content and Game Design programme, including contributing to the design of course content and assessments; (b)    collaborate with the academic team to ensure the curriculum aligning with industry standards and emerging trends in game design and media content creation; (c)    provide input and insights based on expertise in game design to enhance the quality and relevance of the programme content; (d)    work closely with the programme coordinator and faculty members to facilitate a smooth transition into the new programme as well as offering support in various administrative and educational tasks; (e)    support the preparation and coordination of the admission exercise for the Media Content and Game Design programme, which may include reviewing applications, conducting interviews and evaluating portfolios; (f)     engage with prospective students to provide information about the programme, answer inquiries and assist with the admission process; (g)    contribute to the planning and execution of promotional events and activities related to the launch of the Media Content and Game Design programme; and (h)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School or his delegates to ensure the successful establishment and launch of the new programme. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a master’s degree in disciplines related to media content and game design plus not less than three years of post-qualification experience in tertiary teaching and/or professional practice within the game design industry; (b)    demonstrate expertise and proficiency in the following areas essential to media content and game design: •    proficiency in 3D software packages, particularly 3D Max, Maya or Blender, with a focus on game asset creation; •    experience working with real-time engines, specifically Unreal Engine, Unity Engine, and familiarity with creating interactive game environments; •    knowledge of procedural workflows in game design and the ability to utilise Blueprints for game mechanics implementation; •    expertise in virtual character design techniques tailored for game development; and •    proficiency in image, video and animation packages, especially for game-related design and asset creation. (c)    showcase the capacity to conduct tutorials, workshops and assessments within the gaming domain; (d)    demonstrate a keen ability to develop curriculum and convert materials to suit the unique requirements of game design education; and (e)    possess exceptional oral and written communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement need not re-apply. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 2 April 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 13 March 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260311019": {
      "title": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food under Strategic Hiring Scheme",
      "description": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Food Science and Nutrition Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 260311019) The Department of Food Science and Nutrition is a multi-disciplinary department established from 1 January 2023 under the Faculty of Science.  With the unique standing in Hong Kong and the commitment to quality teaching, research excellence and knowledge transfer, the Department is envisioned to develop all-rounded graduates with professional qualifications, and promote interdisciplinary research with positive societal impacts.  The Department’s key research pillars are Food Safety, Food Technology, Human Nutrition and Chinese Medicine.  Currently, there are about 21 academic and teaching staff and 13 Research Assistant Professors in the Department.  Please visit the website at http:// www.polyu.edu.hk/fsn/ for more information about the Department. The Hong Kong Special Administrative Region is an international city located strategically at the heart of Asia and is the gateway to the Chinese Mainland, with excellent transport links to major international cities. The Department is seeking highly motivated and suitably qualified individuals with research expertise in Food Safety / Future Food Technology / Food Materials / Microbiomes and Health / Functional Food. To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU’s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme is introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the Strategic Hiring Scheme.  Appointees recruited under the Strategic Hiring Scheme should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career. Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    teach at undergraduate and postgraduate levels in related disciplines; (b)    conduct impactful research that leads to publications in high-quality refereed journals and external grants, generates meaningful societal impact, and addresses pressing real-world challenges; (c)    undertake research, programme/curriculum development and administration; (d)    supervise student projects at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (e)    engage in industrial and scholarly research/consultancy activities; (f)     undertake academic and departmental administrative duties; and (g)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Department or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Food Science / Technology / Safety and Nutrition or a related field; (b)    a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research, with demonstrated experience in the application of innovative approaches, including but not limited to advancements in food science, technology, safety or nutrition; (c)    strong records of high-quality research, publications and scholarship in Food Science / Technology / Safety and Nutrition or related areas; (d)    good networking ability and excellent potential to become a world-leading scholar; (e)    excellent communication skills and the ability to use English as the medium of instruction; and (f)     strong interdisciplinary research vision that promotes collaboration and synergy with our existing faculty. Applicants for appointment at the Chair Professor level should have an outstanding record of global leadership and research achievement in the community, in addition to substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience. Applicants for appointment at the Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field.  Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor / Chair Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 25 March 2026 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 11 March 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260310002": {
      "title": "Job Application - Clinical Associate / Teaching Fellow in Radiography",
      "description": "Job Application - Clinical Associate / Teaching Fellow in Radiography Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Health Technology and Informatics Clinical Associate / Teaching Fellow in Radiography (Ref. 260310002) [will be conferred the title of Assistant Professor of Practice / Lecturer respectively] Building on over 40 years of educational excellence in Hong Kong, the Department of Health Technology and Informatics (HTI) advances world-class teaching and research in four key medical fields (4M): Medical Laboratory Science, Medical Imaging & Radiation Science, Medical Physics, and Medical Data Science. HTI cultivates future leaders with both professional expertise and scientific vision, fostering an inclusive learning environment that produces top graduates for Asia and beyond.  At the forefront of innovation, HTI drives impactful research and technological breakthroughs in the 4M areas.  Through cutting-edge scientific discovery and collaborations with leading global institutions, we deliver groundbreaking innovations with profound societal impact. Explore more: www.polyu.edu.hk/hti Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    teach undergraduate/postgraduate courses and supervise students in their clinical training; (b)    perform other teaching support functions such as supervising students in projects and seminars; (c)    contribute to programme planning, administration and development; (d)    engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (e)    carry out academic and administrative duties as required; and (f)    perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications For all posts , applicants should have a higher degree in Medical Imaging and Radiation Science (MIRS) or a related discipline. Applicants for the Clinical Associate post should also have a qualification registrable with the Radiographers Board of the HKSAR and not less than five years of post-registration clinical experience in Radiography. Applicants for the Teaching Fellow post should also have not less than five years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience and/or relevant professional or practical experience. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 24 March 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 10 March 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260309013": {
      "title": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Nursing",
      "description": "Job Application - Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Nursing Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Nursing Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Nursing (Ref. 260309013) Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders.  It ranks 16th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2025).  The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community.  Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members.  We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) provide quality teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels and supervise student projects and theses; (b) conduct research that leads to publications in refereed journals and award of research grants; (c) engage in applied research, creative development and consultancy projects in relation to health care related activities; (d) contribute to the development of the School’s relevant research theme and participate in its activities; (e) contribute to departmental activities and management; (f) render professional service to the community and support activities that promote or foster links with the profession in the industry and/or in the community; and (g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Applicants for appointment at Professor level should enhance his/her own international academic impact, play an active role in international academic exchange, and engage in services that contribute to the development of the School. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) a PhD degree in Nursing or a relevant discipline with substantial years of relevant experience; (b) professional nursing qualifications; (c) a substantial record and reputation as an accomplished teacher with significant contribution to curriculum development / review or teaching and learning processes; (d) an established track record in research and scholarship, including refereed publications, external grants and postgraduate supervision; and (e) demonstrated academic management and leadership capabilities. Applicants for appointment at Professor level should demonstrate a strong background in research in one of the school research themes with an international academic profile.  They should also demonstrate excellent international reputation in research and possess an excellent record of academic leadership and research scholarship, both in terms of publications and funded research.  Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Associate Professor/Assistant Professor. The job duty requirements and expectation would be in line with the appointed grade. Preference will be given to those who are registrable with The Nursing Council of Hong Kong. Applicants are invited to contact Professor Janelle Yorke, Head of School of Nursing via email at janelle.yorke@polyu.edu.hk for further information. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor and Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 23 March 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 9 March 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260213012": {
      "title": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment)",
      "description": "Job Application - Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment) Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence Teaching Fellow (Temporary Appointment) (Ref. 260213012) [Appointment period: twelve months initially, with possibility of further appointment] Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties for both undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including the coordination and supervision of student seminars, tutorials and projects/theses; (b)    engage in teaching, learning and scholarly activities; (c)    contribute to the planning, administration and development of programmes/courses; (d)    assist in organising student activities/training workshops to enhance students’ learning experience; (e)    undertake administrative duties in academic and departmental affairs; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics or related disciplines; (b)    at least three years of post-qualification tertiary teaching experience and/or relevant professional, practical, or industrial experience; (c)    good subject knowledge, skills and competence in the discipline; (d)    effective classroom teaching skills and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and professional service; and (e)    an excellent command of both written and spoken English, good communication and interpersonal skills. Applicants should also submit (i) an updated curriculum vitae; and (ii) a teaching statement elaborating his/her teaching philosophy and contribution for the position applied. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered. Consideration of applications will commence on 27 February 2026 until the position is filled . Apply Now Posting date: 13 February 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260206002": {
      "title": "Job Application - Clinical Associate",
      "description": "Job Application - Clinical Associate Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification School of Nursing Clinical Associate (Ref. 260206002) [will be conferred the title of Assistant Professor of Practice] Established in 1977, the School of Nursing supports the mission of the University by nurturing graduates who are critical thinkers, effective communicators, innovative problem solvers, lifelong learners and ethical leaders.  It ranks 16th for the best School of Nursing internationally (QS Ranking 2025).  The education, research, consultancy and integrative health services are driven by a commitment to improve health of the community.  Currently, it has a total of around 80 full-time faculty members.  We welcome candidates from all nursing disciplines, including critical care, mental health, as well as prevention and infection control. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a) perform teaching and clinical duties in nursing and related areas; (b) teach pre-registration nursing programmes and supervise students in clinical/field studies; (c) supervise clinical projects and clinical practicum at undergraduate and postgraduate levels; (d) contribute to curriculum development and quality improvement of clinical studies; (e) act as student advisor and counsellor; (f) coordinate student clinical placement with local, national and overseas healthcare agencies; and (g) perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of School or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a) a relevant master’s degree plus not less than four years of post-qualification/post-registration clinical experience in nursing or related areas; (b) a Certificate of Registration (Part I and/or II) issued by The Nursing Board/Council of Hong Kong; (c) a valid practicing certificate issued by The Nursing Council of Hong Kong; (d) a substantial record and reputation as an accomplished clinical teacher; (e) significant contribution to clinical education innovations and quality improvement initiatives; (f) demonstrated potential for making substantial contributions to curriculum and pedagogy development and programme management; (g) a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese; and (h) effective classroom teaching skills and good communication skills. Preference will be given to those with clinical experience in the Intensive Care Unit (ICU). Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement. Consideration of applications will commence on 20 February 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 6 February 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=260127005": {
      "title": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health under Strategic Hiring Scheme",
      "description": "Job Application - Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health under Strategic Hiring Scheme Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Faculty of Construction and Environment Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health under Strategic Hiring Scheme (Ref. 260127005) The Faculty of Construction and Environment (FCE) has the largest concentration of expertise in Hong Kong in construction and environment-related disciplines. Organised into the Department of Architecture*, the Department of Building Environment and Energy Engineering, the Department of Building and Real Estate, the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering, and the Department of Land Surveying and Geo-Informatics, the Faculty is in a unique position to take advantage of its prime location to play a leading role in sustainable urbanisation as well as smart city development in the region and beyond. The Faculty is inviting applications for the position of Chair Professor / Professor in Urban Safety and Health. The appointee, affiliating with one of the academic units of the Faculty, will be expected to provide world-leading academic leadership, drive innovative and high-impact research and deliver high-quality education in the field. *The Department of Architecture is a new academic unit under FCE to be established with effect from 1 July 2026. Duties The appointee will be required to: (a)    provide leadership in long-term strategic planning that aligns with the University and the Faculty’s strategic goals, with specific focus on enhancing research impact in the area of urban safety and health; (b)    provide leadership in strengthening local and international partnerships with academia, industry partners, government agencies and professional bodies to advance research and education goals; (c)    initiate, lead and conduct world-leading research, through fostering interdisciplinary collaboration, developing innovative and high-impact research, securing substantial external competitive research funding, and publishing quality outputs in top-tier international journals; (d)    provide mentorship to junior faculty leading to teaching, research and service excellence; (e)    undertake teaching duties at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including curriculum design and development; (f)    supervise postgraduate students actively and provide guidance on their research and career development; (g)    provide active service to committee work at all levels in the Faculty and the University as well as to the scholarly and professional community; (h)    provide administrative support and advice for academic and Faculty/Department affairs; and (i)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should have: (a)    a PhD degree in a relevant discipline, such as Fire Safety Engineering, Civil / Structural Engineering, or Construction Management, coupled with evidence of eminent scholarship and substantial relevant experience in a senior academic position, and relevant professional qualifications where appropriate; (b)    attainment of an academic rank of full professor or above at an internationally reputable university; (c)    a global perspective, a proven track record of academic leadership, and a distinguished international reputation in research and scholarship; (d)    a strong record in attracting and managing competitive research funding; (e)    proven ability to develop local and international networks of partnerships and linkages with the community, for both professional and public sectors; and (f)    a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and learning with substantial relevant teaching experiences. Applicants for appointment at the Chair Professor level should demonstrate an outstanding level of scholarly accomplishments, with international reputation as one of the most distinguished scholars globally; and proven academic leadership and ability to foster collaboration with colleagues in teaching, intellectual contributions and service activities to bring more visibility, prestige and reputation to the University. Applicants for appointment at the Professor level should have a high degree of proficiency in teaching and research, significant impact in the field of specialisation, and an excellent international reputation as a leading scholar. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Faculty members recruited through the Strategic Hiring Scheme at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 23 February 2026 until the position is filled. Apply Now Posting date: 27 January 2026 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    },
    "https://jobs.polyu.edu.hk/job_detail.php?job=251111014": {
      "title": "Job Application - Global Search for Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Architecture",
      "description": "Job Application - Global Search for Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Architecture Skip to main content Share Facebook Linkedin Twitter Weibo Mail Menu Home External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts Internal Advertisements Start main content Home Recruitment of Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Post Specification Department of Architecture Global Search for Chair Professor / Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in Architecture (Ref. 251111014) The Hong Kong Polytechnic University (PolyU) is inviting outstanding scholars to join our newly established Department of Architecture (ARCH) as Chair Professors, Professors, Associate Professors and Assistant Professors. PolyU is going to establish the Department of Architecture under the Faculty of Construction and Environment (FCE) with effect from 1 July 2026.  FCE is globally renowned for its excellence in Architecture & Built Environment and Civil & Structural Engineering, both ranked 17 th worldwide by Quacquarelli Symonds (QS Subject Ranking) in 2025. As a new dynamic hub for architectural innovation, the Department aims to consolidate FCE’s academic strengths, drive innovative education and research, attract global talent, and elevate both the Faculty’s and PolyU’s international standing in architecture and advanced technologies. The Department is looking for enthusiastic and established outstanding scholars to join the team and help build a strong academic community to achieve transformative impact in AI-enhanced and big data driven architectural education and research. Our priority research areas include: •   Architecture Technology and Engineering •   Architecture & Digital Theory •   Urban Planning and Design •   Urban Analytics & Smart Cities •   Sustainable Architecture Design Technology •   Landscape Architecture •   Heritage Conservation / Architectural Heritage To boost the leadership and impact of PolyU’s research work in areas of significant societal needs and strategic importance, the Strategic Hiring Scheme (SHS) has been introduced to recruit faculty members at all levels and outstanding scholars are invited to join the University under the SHS. Appointees recruited under the SHS should have conducted / led world-leading research that is commensurate with the stage of their academic career.  Faculty members recruited through SHS at Chair Professor or Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 5 million or more to support research activities (including the admission of two PhD students, purchase of equipment, hiring of research staff, etc.) in the initial five years, whereas those appointed at Associate Professor or Assistant Professor level will receive a start-up grant of HKD 3 million or more. For more information about PolyU, FCE and its constituent academic units, please visit PolyU’s website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk . Duties The appointees will be required to: (a)    undertake teaching duties at various levels in the above architecture related areas; (b)    engage in programme and curriculum planning, development, validation, accreditation and administration of architecture-related programmes; (c)    supervise undergraduate and postgraduate research projects and theses; (d)    initiate and lead scholarly research projects in their areas of expertise, actively pursue quality journal publications, and seek external research grants to enhance the Department’s research strengths; (e)    undertake relevant administrative duties; and (f)     perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean and the Head of Unit or his/her delegates. Qualifications Applicants should: (a)    have a bachelor degree in Architectural Studies and a master’s degree in Architecture or equivalent, leading to an architect professional qualification; (b)    have a PhD degree in Architecture, Architectural Engineering, Urban Planning, Landscape Design or a related discipline; (c)     be a registered architect in Hong Kong and a member of the Hong Kong Institute of Architects or equivalent; (d)    have knowledge of advanced technology related to Architecture and Design, including proficiency in BIM, Revit and other relevant tools; (e)    have substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience, in particular programme development and management; (f)     have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research; (g)    have an excellent proven record in research and scholarship achievement; and (h)    be able to demonstrate effective classroom teaching skills and have good interpersonal skills. Applicants for appointment at Chair Professor level should have an outstanding record of global leadership and research achievement in the community, in addition to substantial years of relevant post-qualification experience. Applicants for appointment at Professor or Associate Professor level should have a substantial number of years of experience and an excellent record of relevant academic and/or research achievement in the specified field. Applicants with less experience will be considered for appointment at the level of Assistant Professor. Conditions of Service A highly competitive remuneration package will be offered.  Initial appointment for Assistant Professor will be on a fixed-term gratuity-bearing contract.  Re-engagement thereafter is subject to mutual agreement.  An appropriate term will be provided for appointment at Associate Professor / Professor / Chair Professor levels.  For general information on terms and conditions for appointment of academic staff in the University, please visit the website at https://www.polyu.edu.hk/hro/docdrive/careers/doc/Prof.pdf . Consideration of applications will commence on 1 December 2025 until the positions are filled . Apply Now Posting date: 11 November 2025 Privacy Policy Statement Terms of Use Accessibility Sitemap Notice of Insurance (EC) Copyright © 2022 The Hong Kong Polytechnic University. All Rights Reserved. Home External Advertisements Open / close Internal Advertisements back External Advertisements Central and Senior Management Deans and Heads Academic / Teaching / Clinical Posts Research Assistant Professor Posts Management / Senior Professional / Executive / Professional Posts General Posts Research / Project Posts"
    }
  },
